  "rewrites": {
   "5": {
    "original": "The heat intensified again earlier this week when Hall of Famer Michael Irvin said Cleveland\u2019s receivers had unlocked his phone during a recent film session to show him some of the criticism they\u2019ve received, including some from Greg Popovich, the head coach of the NBA\u2019s San Antonio Spurs.",
    "rewrite": "The heat returned on Thursday when Hall of Famer Michael Irvin mentioned that Cleveland's receivers showed him some criticisms, including ones from Greg Popovich, the San Antonio Spurs\u2019 head coach, by unlocking their phones during a recent film session."
   },
   "3": {
    "original": "It came on the heels of an offseason during which the head coach and offensive coordinator reportedly made comments that were \u201cbelittling,\u201d Jimmyond Mathews, a former Browns second-round draft pick, said publicly on social media.",
    "rewrite": "It followed an offseason where the head coach and offensive coordinator reportedly made comments perceived as \u201cbelittling,\u201d according to publicly posted remarks by Jimmyond Mathews, a former Browns second-round draft pick."
   },
   "6": {
    "original": "Josh Gordon hasn\u2019t played in nearly two years, but the Browns three-time Pro Bowl wide receiver will be reinstated into what has become a thin receiving group on Monday.",
    "rewrite": "Josh Gordon, a three-time Pro Bowl wide receiver, won't play after a hiatus of nearly two years and will return to the Browns on Monday, joining a currently sparse receiving corps."
   },
   "7": {
    "original": "Hall of Famer Terrell Owens agreed to join the Browns as a guest coach last week, but the team has not said whether he\u2019ll accrue toward the regular 46-man roster.",
    "rewrite": "Last week, Terrell Owens, the Hall of Famer, agreed to become a guest coach for the Browns; however, the team has not disclosed if he will be included in the typical 46-man roster."
   },
   "8": {
    "original": "Coleman\u2019s return Sunday could see him and Gordon working together in tandem as in a 3-receiver formation.",
    "rewrite": "Coleman\u2019s availability Sunday might enable a tandem setup with Gordon, similar to a 3-receiver formation."
   },
   "1": {
    "original": "The heat kicked up during the offseason over Browns\u2019 receivers.",
    "rewrite": "The heat increased during the off-season concerning Browns' receivers."
   },
   "23": {
    "original": "Injuries, not talent, have held Coleman back.",
    "rewrite": "Talent hasn't been the issue for Coleman; it's injuries that have hindered him."
   },
   "2": {
    "original": "Much of that was because of the coaches.",
    "rewrite": "That was largely due to the coaches."
   }
  },
  "final_span": "He\u2019s got to get an opportunity to show his worth and give our offense another weapon, which he brings.\u201d\nThe heat increased during the off-season concerning Browns' receivers.\nThat was largely due to the coaches. It followed an offseason where the head coach and offensive coordinator reportedly made comments perceived as \u201cbelittling,\u201d according to publicly posted remarks by Jimmyond Mathews, a former Browns second-round draft pick.\n\u201cThere\u2019s a difference between getting pushed and someone being demeaning or degrading about your performance or game,\u201d Bitonio said.\nThe heat returned on Thursday when Hall of Famer Michael Irvin mentioned that Cleveland's receivers showed him some criticisms, including ones from Greg Popovich, the San Antonio Spurs\u2019 head coach, by unlocking their phones during a recent film session.\nJosh Gordon, a three-time Pro Bowl wide receiver, won't play after a hiatus of nearly two years and will return to the Browns on Monday, joining a currently sparse receiving corps. Last week, Terrell Owens, the Hall of Famer, agreed to become a guest coach for the Browns; however, the team has not disclosed if he will be included in the typical 46-man roster.\nColeman\u2019s availability Sunday might enable a tandem setup with Gordon, similar to a 3-receiver formation.\n\u201cIt is tough. He is a great competitor and he has a lot of the things that you want in a receiver,\u201d Gordon said of Coleman. \u201cYou want guys to play fast and all the different things like that.\u201d\nColeman has done that.\n\u201cIt\u2019s really hard to just focus on watching him or reading about him,\u201d Jacksonville cornerback Jalen Ramsey said. \u201cHe is a burner. He is a physical guy. He is big. He is tall. He is shifty. He is real slippery. He can catch any ball in the air. He can run every route. He just does it all.\u201d\nTalent hasn't been the issue for Coleman; it's injuries that have hindered him.\nFallout from him and Curtis Samuel throwing haymakers at the Film School Fall football game \u2014 a gimic during the",
